A multi-module repo (no go.work) with two independent modules: a benign root
module example.com/foo and a vulnerable child module example.com/foo/sub that
imports golang.org/x/text v0.3.5 and calls language.Parse (fixed in v0.3.7).
The desired remediation bumps the child module to v0.3.7.
EXPECTED: FAIL. The bot runs `govulncheck ./...` and `go mod tidy` at the repo
root only; the nested module under sub/ is excluded from the root's ./...
package pattern, so the child is never scanned or fixed and the real script
produces an empty diff.
-- go.mod --
module example.com/foo

go 1.25.0
-- main.go --
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
	fmt.Println("hello from the benign root module")
}
-- sub/go.mod --
module example.com/foo/sub

go 1.25.0

require golang.org/x/text v0.3.5
-- sub/lib.go --
package sub

import (
	"fmt"

	"golang.org/x/text/language"
)

// ParseTag calls language.Parse, which in golang.org/x/text v0.3.5 has an
// out-of-bounds read that can panic (a DoS) on malformed BCP 47 input.
func ParseTag(s string) string {
	tag, err := language.Parse(s)
	if err != nil {
		return fmt.Sprintf("error: %v", err)
	}
	return tag.String()
}
